## Current Known Limitation: DSN Exposure

The WebSocket query message includes the raw Postgres DSN:
```json
{ "type": "query", "query": "...", "dsn": "postgresql://user:pass@host/db" }
```

This is an SSRF risk — a malicious user could target internal network hosts.

The fix (Plan 4): store DSNs server-side, issue `connection_id`, use that in query messages.
Until then: only expose to trusted users (single-user local setup is safe).
